<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan sees c/a deficit at $3.6 bln in '97/98.</title>
<headline>Pakistan sees c/a deficit at $3.6 bln in '97/98.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan expects its current account deficit to drop to $3.6 billion in fiscal 1997/98 (July-June) from an estimated $4.3 billion in 1996/97, a government document said.</p>
<p>The Annual Plan for 1997/98, a copy of which was obtained by Reuters on Friday, said the current account deficit would fall largely because of an expected reduction in the trade gap.</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
